hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27405","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah from Ibn Abbas from his mother, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib: By those sent forth in succession."
"27406","Affan said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, that he broke his fast at Arafah; he was brought pomegranate and ate it, and he said: Umm al-Fadl narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast at Arafah; she brought him milk and he drank it."
"27407","Yaqub said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me from Ikrimah, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Abbas from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Umm Habibah bint Abbas, and she was above the age of weaning. She said: So he said: If this little daughter of al-Abbas lives and I am alive, I will marry her."
"27408","Musa ibn Dawud said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us from Humayd from Anas from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in his house, wrapped in a garment, at Maghrib, and he recited: By those sent forth. He did not pray any prayer after it until he passed away (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27409","Sufyan from Abu al-Nadr, he said: I heard Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, mother of the sons of al-Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl, she said: They doubted about the fast of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah, so Umm al-Fadl said: I will find out that for you. So she sent milk, and he drank."
"27410","Ismail said: Ayyub narrated to us from Abu al-Khalil from Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Hashimi from Umm al-Fadl, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, and a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had a wife, then I married another wife besides her, and my first wife claimed that she suckled my new wife one or two sucklings - and he said once: one suckling or two sucklings. So he said: One suckling does not make unlawful, nor two sucklings - or he said: one suckling or two sucklings."
"27411","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai said: Layth informed us, and Yunus said: Layth - meaning Ibn Sad - narrated to us from Yazid ibn al-Had from Hind bint al-Harith from Umm al-Fadl, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon al-Abbas while he was complaining, and he wished for death, so he said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, do not wish for death; if you are a doer of good, increasing good upon your good is better for you, and if you are a doer of evil, then being delayed so you may seek amends is better for you, so do not wish for death. Yunus said: And if you are a doer of evil, then being delayed so you may seek amends from your evil is better for you."
"27412","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr said: Israil narrated to us from Simak from Qabus ibn Abi al-Mukhariq from Umm al-Fadl, she said: I saw as if in my house there was a limb from the limbs of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: So I was alarmed by that, and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Good; Fatimah will give birth to a boy, and you will sponsor him with the milk of your son Qutham. She said: So she gave birth to Hasan, and he was given to me, and I suckled him until he moved - or: I weaned him - then I came with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and seated him in his lap, and he urinated, so I struck between his shoulders, so he said: Be gentle with my son, may Allah have mercy on you - or: may Allah make you righteous - you have pained my son. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, take off your waist-wrapper and wear another garment until I wash it. He said: The urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled."
"27413","Abu Mamar - and I heard it myself from Abu Mamar - said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Yazid - meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad - narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, and she is the mother of the child of al-Abbas, sister of Maymunah, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness and began weeping, so he raised his head and said: What makes you weep? I said: We feared for you, and we do not know what we will meet from the people after you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You are the oppressed after me."
"27414","Affan and Bahz said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed us from Lubabah Umm al-Fadl, that she used to suckle al-Hasan or al-Husayn. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and lay down in a sprinkled place, and she placed him on his belly, and he urinated on his belly, and I saw the urine flowing on his belly, so I stood to a waterskin to pour it over him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm al-Fadl, the urine of a boy has water poured over it, and the urine of a girl is washed. And Bahz said: washing."
"27415","Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Humayd: Ata used to narrate it from Abu Ata from Lubabah."
"27416","Affan said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Salih Abu al-Khalil from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Umm al-Fadl, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw in my dream that in my house - or my chamber - there was a limb from your limbs. He said: Fatimah will give birth, if Allah wills, to a boy, and you will sponsor him. So Fatimah gave birth to Hasan, and she handed him to her, and she suckled him with the milk of Qutham. And I came with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day visiting him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him and placed him on his chest, and he urinated on his chest, and the urine reached his waist-wrapper, so I struck with my hand on his shoulders, so he said: You have pained my son, may Allah make you righteous - or he said: may Allah have mercy on you. So I said: Give me your waist-wrapper to wash it. So he said: The urine of a girl is washed, and water is poured over the urine of a boy."
"27417","Abu Kamil said: Hammad narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu al-Khalil from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Umm al-Fadl, that the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling does not make unlawful, nor two sucklings."
"27418","Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Ibn Abbas from his mother Umm al-Fadl, she said: The last I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he recited in Maghrib Surah al-Mursalat."
"27419","Yahya ibn Said from Malik: Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to me from Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, that Umm al-Fadl informed him that they doubted about the fast of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah, so she sent to him milk, and he drank while he was addressing the people at Arafah on his camel."
"27420","Hajjaj said: Sharik narrated to us from Simak ibn Harb from Qabus ibn Mukhariq from Umm al-Fadl, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then she mentioned something like the hadith of Affan. He said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Salih Abu al-Khalil, then he mentioned something like it."
"27421","Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan narrated to us from Salim Abu al-Nadr from Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, from Umm al-Fadl, that they disputed about the fast of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah, so she sent to him a cup containing milk, and he drank it."
"27422","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, and Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, the meaning, from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith heard him while he was reciting: By those sent forth in succession. So she said: O my son, by Allah, you have reminded me by this recitation of yours of this surah; it is the last I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib."
"27423","Bahz ibn Asad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas, that he broke his fast at Arafah. He said: And Umm al-Fadl narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast at Arafah; she brought him milk and he drank it."
"27424","Bahz and Affan said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu al-Khalil from Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does one suck make unlawful? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. And Affan said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, then he mentioned it."
